        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Fangs (1974)** (1974) represents a fascinating entry in the wave of exploitation snake films that slithered through drive-ins in the 1970s. Following the massive success of <a href=\"/movie/42532\" class=\"movie-title\">Willard</a> (1971) with its killer rats, producers rushed to capitalize on animal attack films. **Fangs** took inspiration from both the creature feature tradition and the emerging environmental horror subgenre pioneered by films like **Frogs** (1972). The film's focus on a small town terrorized by venomous snakes tapped into primal fears while reflecting growing concerns about humanity's impact on nature."
